  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday Night through Saturday)\nIssued at 1144 PM CDT Sat Oct 10 2026\n\nThe unseasonable warmth will continue Monday and Tuesday, with\nnear record high temperatures expected. Gusty south winds will\ncontinue, with heightened fire weather concerns at least on\nMonday. A substantial increase in humidity values Tuesday along\nwith increased cloud cover will likely keep fire weather concerns\nin check compared to Monday.\n\nMultiple rounds of showers and thunderstorms are expected Tuesday\nnight through Thursday in association with an upper trough over\nthe western U.S. and a stalled out frontal boundary near the\nOklahoma/Kansas border. Locally heavy rainfall will be possible,\nespecially across the northern part of the forecast area, and a\nlimited severe weather threat may also develop during this time\nframe. A stronger cold front will then push south across the area\nlate Thursday and Thursday night, with rain chances diminishing\nfollowing the frontal passage.\n\nMuch cooler and drier weather will follow this front Friday into\nnext weekend, with temperatures near or even a bit below the\nseasonal averages.",
